## FILTERING & ENRICHMENT LAYER

### Step 1: Apply Filters
```
For each collected job:
  - Check title against ROLES list → Pass/Fail
  - Check location against LOCATIONS list → Pass/Fail
  - Check description for SOFTWARE keywords (Avid, Premiere) → Flag as priority if found
  
  Keep job if: (Title match) AND (Location match)
  Optional boost: Add software match flag for ranking
```

### Step 2: Generate Personalized Outreach Materials

**A. Short Message (Under 150 characters):**
```
Template:
"Hi [COMPANY], I'm interested in the [TITLE] role. With my editing experience [+ software if known], 
I'd love to contribute to your projects. Check out my work: [PORTFOLIO_URL or CONTACT_INFO]"

Logic:
- Extract company name from job listing
- Insert job title
- Conditionally add "with Avid/Premiere Pro experience" if software detected
- Truncate to 150 chars if exceeds limit
```

**B. Cover Letter (500 characters, semi-personalized):**
```
Template:
"Dear [COMPANY] Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the [TITLE] position in [LOCATION]. With my background 
in post-production editing, including experience with [DETECTED_SOFTWARE or "Avid and Premiere Pro"], 
I am confident I can contribute effectively to your [CONTENT_TYPE] productions.

[RESUME_SNIPPET from PDF - first 300 chars of relevant experience]

I look forward to discussing how my skills align with your needs.

Best regards,
[USER_NAME]"

Logic:
- Extract company, title, location from job data
- Detect software from job description, insert if found
- Parse user's resume PDF to extract text snippet
- Generate personalized cover letter truncated to 500 chars
```

### Step 3: Resume PDF Extraction
- Read user's resume PDF (config path: resume.pdf)
- Extract first 1000 characters of text (PyPDF2 library)
- Use in cover letter generation for personalization
- Fallback if PDF unreadable: Default text "Assistant Editor with experience in Avid and Premiere Pro"

